# Skinwise — environment variables
#
# THE FIVE THAT MATTER IN PRODUCTION. Set these in the Vercel project
# (Settings → Environment Variables → Production), then redeploy:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL     Supabase project URL
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY    server-only; the ONLY database credential
#   OPENAI_API_KEY               server-only; text + vision + STT + TTS
#   ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN           server-only; expert console login
#   CRON_SECRET                  server-only; photo-retention purge job
#
# Everything else below is an optional model/voice override with a working
# default. The app builds, deploys and serves every public page with NONE of
# these set — each dependent feature degrades to a stated WhatsApp handoff
# rather than a crash or a false success. That is deliberate, and it is what
# a deployment with no variables configured is actually doing.
#
# There is no anon key. Reads and writes go through the service role on the
# server only: RLS is enabled with zero policies, so a leaked browser-side
# key would grant nothing, and none is shipped. Never prefix a secret with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that inlines it into the client bundle.
#
# Placeholders only. Never commit a real value; .env.local is gitignored.

# --- Stage 2: Skin Check persistence ---------------------------------
# Until these are set, POST /api/v1/assessments/submit returns
# { status: "fallback" } and the UI hands the user to WhatsApp rather than
# showing a success screen for a lead nobody received. See
# lib/assessment/storage.ts.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=        # safe for the browser
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=       # SERVER ONLY. Never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# --- Stage 3.2: internal expert/admin workspace ----------------------
# Shared secret exchanged for a signed httpOnly session cookie by
# /api/v1/admin/login; middleware.ts gates every /admin route with it.
# Interim single-team-token auth, to be replaced by per-expert Supabase
# Auth. Placeholder only — never commit a real value.
# ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- Stage 4: AI text assistant --------------------------------------
# Anthropic Messages API key (server-only). Without it, /api/v1/assistant
# degrades to a WhatsApp handoff rather than failing. Recommended model is
# claude-haiku-4-5 for a grounded product-Q&A assistant. Placeholder only.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Stage 4: OpenAI (preferred provider) ----------------------------
# OpenAI Chat Completions key (server-only). Selected before Anthropic
# when both are present. Default model gpt-4.1-mini, overridable via
# OPENAI_MODEL. Without any AI key, /api/v1/assistant degrades to a
# WhatsApp handoff. Placeholder only — never commit a real value.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini

# --- Stage 5: skin analyzer (vision) ---------------------------------
# Reuses OPENAI_API_KEY. Vision model overridable (default gpt-4.1-mini,
# which supports image input + strict structured output).
# OPENAI_VISION_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini

# --- Stage 6: voice agent (reuses OPENAI_API_KEY) --------------------
# STT (server fallback; browser Web Speech API is primary) + TTS. All
# overridable; all reuse the OpenAI key. Without a key, voice degrades to
# the text assistant's not-configured handling.
# OPENAI_STT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-transcribe
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=shimmer

# --- Stage 8: operations ---------------------------------------------
# Bearer secret for the photo-retention purge cron (/api/v1/cron/purge-
# photos). Vercel Cron sends it automatically; without it the route
# refuses to run. Generate a long random value. Placeholder only.
# CRON_SECRET=
